From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:32:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 45/46] e2e: block I/O in whole sectors; FreeBSD sector size
 and ext fs name

A raw disk (FreeBSD has no buffered block devices) reads and writes whole
sectors only: the block read and write helpers now use whole 512-byte
sectors (padding writes with zeros, checking the first bytes read),
which a Linux block device accepts the same way. On FreeBSD nodes the
sector size is md(4)'s 512 (no blockdev) and an ext2/3/4 volume is
listed as ext2fs.
---
 test/e2e/framework/volume/fixtures.go | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++------
 test/e2e/storage/utils/utils.go       | 24 ++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/test/e2e/framework/volume/fixtures.go b/test/e2e/framework/volume/fixtures.go
